{
  "summary": "Extracts `-signetchallenge` parsing and hex validation into a shared `ReadSignetChallengeArg()` helper in `chainparamsbase`. Calls this helper from both `GetSignetDataDir()` and `ReadSigNetArgs()`, ensuring `bitcoin-cli` immediately rejects invalid hex or duplicate challenge arguments instead of failing later during RPC authentication.",
  "problem": "When invalid hex or duplicate values are supplied to `-signetchallenge` in `bitcoin-cli`, the CLI tool does not validate the argument during data directory resolution. It silently falls back to the default signet datadir and eventually fails with an unhelpful authorization or missing RPC cookie error rather than reporting the malformed argument.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description demonstrates the error discrepancy: `bitcoind -signet -signetchallenge=z` reports `Error: -signetchallenge must be hex, not 'z'`, while `bitcoin-cli` only fails later with `error: Authorization failed... Is your -signetchallenge correct for custom signets?`",
    "Addressed review feedback from merged PR #34566: 'Addresses https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34566#discussion_r3668123074'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "",
  "changed_since_previous": "Dropped the helper function casing rename to `SigNet`, retaining `ReadSignetChallengeArg` with standard `Signet` casing.",
  "card": "Unifies -signetchallenge argument validation between bitcoind and bitcoin-cli by moving hex checking into a shared helper function. Currently, passing invalid hex or multiple challenge values to bitcoin-cli fails late with an ambiguous RPC authorization error instead of pinpointing the bad input. With this change, bitcoin-cli throws an immediate error on malformed or duplicate challenge arguments matching the error output of bitcoind.",
